app.degraded	app entered degraded (observe window failure / post-window instability / W_DEPLOY_INSTABILITY)
app.deleted	app deletion completed (tombstone second beat: managed services removed, name enters retention hold)
app.instability_detected	instability detected at runtime
app.recovered	app left degraded, back to running
app.substrate_missing	app claimed running but its managed service(s) are absent from the substrate (external removal); view corrected to down
app.webhook_fetch_failed	async source fetch failed after webhook acceptance (retry manually via redeliver on the same delivery)
backup.upload_failed	remote state backup upload failed (local snapshot unaffected; payload carries the backup id and a redacted error summary, never credentials)
backup.upload_recovered	remote state backup upload recovered (previous upload had failed; payload carries the backup id)
build.stale_nonterminal	build stayed queued/building past 2x the build timeout budget (surfaces state-machine bugs; no self-healing)
cron.failed	cron run failed (task failed/rejected; no retry — restart-condition=none; job service removed)
cron.skipped	cron trigger skipped (overlap / node unavailable / missed during downtime / interrupted by restart); no catch-up run
cron.succeeded	cron run completed (task complete; job service removed)
cron.timed_out	cron run exceeded its watchdog budget (default 10m, fleetly.cron.timeout label overrides; job service removed)
cron.triggered	cron schedule fired: one-shot swarm job created (payload carries app/service/run id/job service; scheduled_at is the hit cron point)
db.backup_failed	database backup failed (failure summary in payload, never credentials)
db.backup_succeeded	database backup succeeded (ledger row written; verify pending)
db.credentials_rotated	database credentials rotated (manual two-phase confirm; referencing apps auto-redeploy follows)
db.degraded	database in service turned unhealthy (health probe failing / task crash loop; swarm self-healing observed)
db.delete_started	database deletion accepted (reference guard passed; tombstone first beat)
db.deleted	database deletion completed (managed objects reaped; name enters retention hold; volumes orphaned by default)
db.provision_failed	database convergence failed (health gate timeout / image unavailable / engine error; scene preserved, explicit retry required)
db.provision_started	database provisioning/convergence started (create, resume or retry acceptance; state -> provisioning)
db.ready	database passed the health gate (provisioning -> ready)
db.recovered	database recovered (health probe passing again; degraded -> ready)
db.restore_completed	database restore completed in place (confirm-gated destructive operation)
db.restore_failed	database restore failed (critical alert; in-place replay interrupted)
db.resumed	database resume accepted (paused -> provisioning reconvergence)
db.suspended	database suspended (scale 0, services and volumes retained)
db.upgrade_available	newer template image digest available for the database template (opt-in upgrade advertised)
db.upgrade_failed	database upgrade failed (digest rolled back to the previous value; state degraded)
db.upgrade_finished	database upgrade finished (new digest converged and healthy)
db.upgrade_started	database upgrade started (pre_upgrade backup gate begins; controlled rebuild)
deployment.cancelled	deploy cancelled (replays the prior state first, then lands cancelled)
deployment.failed	deploy failed (terminal state; reason=error code)
deployment.healthy	new revision passed the health gate
deployment.observe_started	observe window started (default 60s)
deployment.queued	deploy queued (per-app mutually exclusive queueing)
deployment.recovery_blocked	recovery blocked (e.g. bound node unavailable)
deployment.recovery_scheduled	recovery from systemic failure queued (automatic retry action)
deployment.release_started	release started (build/update kicking off)
deployment.rollback_failed	rollback failed
deployment.rollback_finished	rollback finished
deployment.rollback_started	rollback started (single-layer replay of the revision)
deployment.substrate_halted	substrate failure halted the deploy (Swarm/node unavailable)
deployment.succeeded	deploy succeeded (terminal state)
deployment.superseded	deploy superseded by a newer target (stale terminal state)
deployment.switched	traffic switch completed
deployment.warning	deploy warning (W_ code; observe window alert-only semantics)
engine.stale_nonterminal	deploy stayed non-terminal past 2x the (deploy watchdog + observe window) budget (surfaces state-machine bugs; no self-healing)
git.hostkey_changed	the git SSH host key changed since the previous load (file rebuilt or key replaced; payload carries the old and new SHA256 fingerprints — public key material only, the private key never appears)
invite.accepted	a one-time team invite was accepted (payload carries team_id/user_id/role; the plaintext token never appears anywhere)
logs.backend_updated	log backend setting changed (payload carries the backend value; switch triggers the duty to deploy or remove VictoriaLogs, the data volume is retained)
logs.ingest_degraded	log ingestion to VictoriaLogs degraded (backend unreachable; live tail unaffected; payload carries dropped_total and a single-line error summary)
logs.ingest_recovered	log ingestion to VictoriaLogs recovered (degradation streak exited)
logs.victorialogs_deployed	managed VictoriaLogs deployed or converged to the desired spec (payload carries service/image/reason)
logs.victorialogs_removed	managed VictoriaLogs removed after logs.backend left victorialogs (data volume retained; payload carries volume_retained=true)
metrics.mode_updated	metrics mode setting changed (payload carries the mode value; switching on deploys the managed VictoriaMetrics/cAdvisor/node-exporter stack, switching off removes the services — the data volume is retained)
metrics.stack_deployed	managed metrics stack service deployed or converged to the desired spec (payload carries service/image/reason)
metrics.stack_removed	managed metrics stack removed after metrics.mode left on (data volume retained; payload carries volume_retained=true)
network.missing	an expected project network is absent from the substrate (external removal); disclosed only — the next attach or member deploy re-ensures it
network.orphaned	a platform-managed fleetly- network exists that no state fact attributes to a live resource (unattributed leak; disclosed only — never deleted silently)
node.availability_changed	node availability changed (active/drain/pause transition; drain maintenance-window narrative; payload carries old/new)
node.down	node judged DOWN (Swarm loss-of-contact verdict)
node.joined	node joined the cluster (observed)
node.removed	node removed (observed docker node rm)
node.up	node back to ready
placement.blocked	bound node unavailable/removed; app blocked
placement.bound	app node binding completed (including automatic pinning)
placement.changed	binding changed (via the explicitly confirmed migration path)
placement.recovered	bound node recovered; binding re-established automatically
placement.unresolved	binding undecidable after DR; explicit placement required (no guessing)
project.created	a project was created (payload carries team_id/slug; W1 source = the default project provisioned atomically with registration, W2-S1 source = ProjectsService.CreateProject)
project.deleted	an empty project was deleted (non-empty guard passed; payload carries team_id/slug)
project.member_changed	a project role override was set or removed (payload carries change/user_id and role on override_set; no row means the team role applies again)
project.network_changed	an app was attached to or detached from its project network (payload carries change/app/app_id/project_id; participation is an explicit opt-in and defaults off)
reconcile.drift_detected	drift detected between desired and actual state (including manual docker operations); convergence is per-app opt-in
registry.updated	platform registry credentials changed (payload carries the host and the password fingerprint, never credentials)
release.job_failed	release-time init job failed (task failed/rejected/shut down; the deployment fails — no retry, restart-condition=none; job service removed)
release.job_timed_out	release-time init job exceeded its watchdog budget (default 10m, fleetly.job.timeout label overrides; the deployment fails and the job service is removed)
restore.completed	control plane restore completed (after exiting read-only observation)
route.label_ignored	compose fleetly.domains label declarations were ignored because state domain rows exist (labels are bootstrap-only; payload carries the declared/state counts)
route.publish_failed	app ingress route publish failed (deploy unaffected; alerts separately)
route.published	app ingress routes published (after the health gate passed, all dynamic config converged)
s3.rustfs_deployed	managed RustFS deployed or converged to the desired spec (payload carries service/image/reason, never credentials)
s3.rustfs_removed	managed RustFS removed after s3.mode left rustfs (data volume retained; payload carries volume_retained=true)
s3.updated	object storage settings changed (payload carries the mode and toggles, never credentials)
scaling.adjusted	autoscaler adjusted a service's replica count (payload carries the triggering dimension, before/after replicas and measured utilization)
scaling.dormant	a scaling policy is dormant because metrics.mode is not on (one-time disclosure per policy; re-armed when metrics turns on)
scaling.no_data	a scaling policy had no metric series for its target dimension — no action, honest no-data (one-time disclosure per policy)
task.created	dynamic task accepted (owner token recorded; the engine converges the substrate service next; payload carries image/scope/network/ttl, never env values)
task.deleted	dynamic task ledger row removed (substrate service already removed)
task.expired	dynamic task TTL elapsed: the janitor reclaims the substrate service and lands the task stopped
task.failed	dynamic task failed (substrate convergence failure, image unavailable, or the container task failed/rejected — restart-condition none means the platform does not self-heal it; payload carries a bounded error summary)
task.orphaned	a platform-managed task service has no non-terminal state row (leftover or externally created): disclosed and reclaimed (the platform owns the object; label attribution)
task.started	dynamic task converged: the substrate service is in place and resolvable by its stable DNS name inside the scope network
task.stopped	dynamic task stopped and its substrate service removed (payload carries reason: owner | expired | exited)
team.created	a team was created (payload carries slug/name; W1 source = the personal team provisioned atomically with registration, W2-S1 source = TeamsService.CreateTeam)
team.member_changed	team membership changed — a member added, role changed or removed (payload carries change/user_id/role or from/to; removal carries the purged project-override count)
terminal.closed	web terminal session closed (payload carries duration, close code and reason; metadata only, never session content)
terminal.opened	web terminal session opened (payload carries app/service/container/node/token metadata only, never session content)
user.registered	a user completed self-registration (payload carries email/is_platform_admin/team_id/team_slug, never credentials; first user is platform admin with a personal team + default project)
volume.created	volume registered (data birthplace; pins the hosting node)
volume.detached	volume detached (volume declaration removed; data is not deleted with the declaration)
volume.discarded	volume explicitly discarded (admin+confirm+audited)
volume.orphaned	volume orphaned (old volume kept by default after app deletion / after --discard)
